text:
maria: Heads up: onboarding sample-app shows different behavior between go-sdk and web-client for streaming long responses. Go reassembles and finishes, browser stops early ~10% of runs.
aj: repro? stack/traces?
maria: small harness in examples/streaming-shim. Steps: start local proxy, open sample page, feed a long prompt. Browser console shows `SSE closed unexpectedly` and UI shows partial JSON. Go test logs show resume-token received then final event.
lee: any chance this is last-event-id handling? EventSource automatically sets Last-Event-ID header sometimes.
maria: we log these on the runtime side:
```
[2034-12-01T14:02:11.100Z] runtime: emit seq=12 resume=tok-45 data=...
[2034-12-01T14:02:11.200Z] runtime: keepalive empty event
[2034-12-01T14:02:11.201Z] proxy: injected CRLF (client-abort path)
[2034-12-01T14:02:11.202Z] runtime: emit seq=13 resume=tok-46 data=...
[2034-12-01T14:02:11.203Z] client: EventSource.onerror -> closed
```
aj: so proxy CRLF between keepalive and actual token triggers onerror in some browsers. Go client tolerates it. We need a cross-SDK mitigation.
lee: SDK parity checklist item: make all official SDKs ignore pure empty events, and require explicit `event: resume` or `event: final` markers for finalization.
maria: propose: runtime emits `event: keepalive` for heartbeats instead of blank lines, and `event: done` with final seq+resume. That avoids ambiguity.
aj: nice. Also add a small patch in web-sample: only treat onerror->close as fatal after a 150ms grace period (allows short reconnects / auth refresh to avoid premature close).
lee: caution: adding grace can mask genuine disconnects and increase perceived latency. Make it opt-in for sample-app only, and recommend app-level approach in README.
infra-bot: CI: created ticket INFRA-987 to investigate proxy CRLF injection and add logging.
ci-bot: CI: ran streaming-shim e2e across browsers: Chrome 100/100 on patched runtime+shim, Firefox 98/100 (2 flakes).
aj: for SDKs, also add small reassembly helper that accepts partial JSON across SSE chunks. Example helper for browser: ```js
let buf = '';
eventSource.onmessage = (e) => {
  buf += e.data;
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(buf);
    handle(obj);
    buf = '';
  } catch (err) {
    // wait for more chunks
  }
}
```
lee: add test harness that simulates split JSON across keepalive + token boundaries + resume token mismatch.
maria: I'll update sample-app, runtime proposal, and add a DX note about Last-Event-ID differences + why clients should rely on explicit resume events.
aj: sounds good. can we also warn in the SDK docs that some CDNs/proxies may normalize CRLFs and that can create phantom empty events? small note under "Streaming pitfalls".
lee: agreed. I'll open SDK parity PRs after infra ticket lands.
ci-bot: CI: merged small shim into sample-app branch, queued runtime RFC.
maria: thanks everyone, will follow up with RFC link and a short blog blurb for onboarding teams. :rocket:
